---
---
<section class="section" id="pathway">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">06 · Development Pathway</span>
      <h2>Pathways teams can take</h2>
      <p>
        AKD supports two parallel development pathways depending on whether an agent needs
        custom tools, APIs, or integrations. Both begin with the CARE design methodology.
        Approved agents are distributed across multiple endpoints — Flow, Custom GPT directory,
        community MCP servers, and the akd-ext open-source repo — not just one.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="pathway-services" aria-label="AKD services available to teams">
      <div class="services-head">
        <span class="services-eyebrow">AKD services NASA teams can use</span>
        <p>
          Governance and safety services come built in — available across every stage of the pathway. Teams pick what they need; the list below is a non-exhaustive sample, not an ordered priority.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="services-list">
        <li>
          <b>Reusable Scientific Tools</b>
          <span>MCP-wrapped search, retrieval, and analysis tools agents compose instead of re-implementing.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>FactReasoner</b>
          <span>Targeted factuality reasoning over claims, attribution, and supporting evidence in agent outputs.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Risk Agent</b>
          <span>LLM-judge evaluating outputs against the IBM Risk Atlas and the NASA-IMPACT Science Literature Risk taxonomy.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Compliance Checking</b>
          <span>Automated guardrail layer enforcing science-specific constraints on inputs and outputs.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Science Guardrails (umbrella)</b>
          <span>Defense-in-depth: layered input, intermediate-step, and output verification — not a single gate.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Granite Guardian</b>
          <span>Foundation-model content moderation — jailbreak, harm, bias, plus RAG groundedness checks. Runs via Ollama.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </aside>

    <div class="pathway-diagram" aria-label="Agent development pathways">

      <!-- Row 0: Common start -->
      <div class="pathway-row pathway-row--start">
        <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--featured">
          <span>Phase 1 · All Agents</span>
          <b>Design (CARE)</b>
          <p class="pipe-desc">
            Every agent starts here. SMEs, developers, and helper LLM agents work through
            five CARE phases — scope, key-information elicitation, reasoning policy,
            implementation, and benchmarking — passing a stage gate at each step and
            producing reusable design artifacts before any code is written.
          </p>
          <p class="gov-tag"><span>Governance:</span> CARE phase gates — joint SME / developer / agent approval at each phase</p>
          <a class="pipe-link" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd-suite/tree/main/akd-care" target="_blank" rel="noopener">akd-care ↗</a>
        </div>
        <div class="fork-indicator" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="fork-line fork-line--left"></span>
          <span class="fork-node">↓ choose path</span>
          <span class="fork-line fork-line--right"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Row 1: Two branches -->
      <div class="pathway-row pathway-row--branches">

        <!-- Branch A: Simple Agents -->
        <div class="branch branch--simple">
          <div class="branch-label">Tool-Independent</div>
          <div class="pipe-step">
            <span>Phase 2a · Simple Agents</span>
            <b>Custom GPT</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Paste the CARE-developed system prompt as GPT instructions, upload domain
              context documents, and select the model. No custom code required. Examples:
              Scientific Illustrator, Paper Writing Assistant, NASA Data Governance agent.
            </p>
            <p class="gov-tag"><span>Governance:</span> Public-use policy approval; baseline guardrail prompt patterns embedded by CARE</p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd-suite/tree/main/agents" target="_blank" rel="noopener">agents/ ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Branch B: Tool-Integrated Agents -->
        <div class="branch branch--tool">
          <div class="branch-label">Tool-Integrated</div>
          <div class="pipe-step">
            <span>Phase 2b · Tool-Integrated Agents</span>
            <b>Build in akd-ext</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Implement the agent using the OpenAIBaseAgent pattern in akd-ext: author tool
              wrappers, MCP integrations, and API clients. Examples: Earth Science Data
              Search (CMR), Code Search, Astro Data Search.
            </p>
            <p class="gov-tag"><span>Governance:</span> Tools whitelist; static MCP-server config; guardrail integration required</p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd-suite/tree/main/akd-ext" target="_blank" rel="noopener">akd-ext ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
          <div class="pipe-step">
            <span>Phase 3b</span>
            <b>Test &amp; Iterate in AKD Labs</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Chat-test the agent in the Chat Playground, inspect full trace logs, refine
              system prompts and tool configurations, and run benchmarks against a
              prepared test suite. Experimental agents remain internal.
            </p>
            <p class="gov-tag"><span>Governance:</span> Internal-only scope; benchmark thresholds enforced before review</p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://labs.akd.odsi.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">labs.akd.odsi.io ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
          <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--gov-gate">
            <span>Phase 4b</span>
            <b>SME Review Gate</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              An SME lead conducts a readiness review verifying scientific integrity
              (non-prescriptive behavior, traceable reasoning), guardrail compliance, and
              benchmark results before promotion to Flow is approved.
            </p>
            <p class="gov-tag gov-tag--strong"><span>Governance:</span> This stage <em>is</em> the gate — no agent reaches Flow without SME sign-off</p>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
          <div class="pipe-step">
            <span>Phase 5b</span>
            <b>Publish to AKD Flow</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Approved agents are published to AKD Flow and to the akd-ext code
              repository, making them available in the workflow canvas for scientists
              to compose into multi-agent pipelines.
            </p>
            <p class="gov-tag"><span>Governance:</span> Operational guardrails active in production; HITL checkpoints in every workflow run</p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://flow.akd.odsi.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">flow.akd.odsi.io ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Row 2: Distribution endpoints -->
      <div class="pathway-row pathway-row--end">
        <div class="merge-indicator" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="fork-line fork-line--left"></span>
          <span class="fork-node">↓ distribute</span>
          <span class="fork-line fork-line--right"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="endpoints-grid">
          <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--endpoint">
            <span class="endpoint-tag">Endpoint</span>
            <b>AKD Flow Workflows</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Composed multi-agent pipelines on the AKD Flow canvas — scientists
              assemble approved agents, run workflows with streaming updates and
              guardrail badges, and share reproducible results.
            </p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://flow.akd.odsi.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">flow.akd.odsi.io ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--endpoint">
            <span class="endpoint-tag">Endpoint</span>
            <b>Custom GPT Directory</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Tool-independent agents published directly as Custom GPTs using the
              CARE-developed system prompt — no custom code required. Examples:
              Scientific Illustrator, Paper Writing Assistant, Data Governance Agent.
            </p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd-suite/tree/main/agents" target="_blank" rel="noopener">agents/ ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--endpoint">
            <span class="endpoint-tag">Endpoint</span>
            <b>Community MCP Servers</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Teams hosting their own MCP servers with agents that integrate via the
              AKD framework. Community-contributed agents are governed by the same
              CARE and SME-review process as first-party agents.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--endpoint">
            <span class="endpoint-tag">Endpoint</span>
            <b>akd-ext Open-Source Repo</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Published agent code on GitHub — available for forking, peer review,
              and integration into other projects. The canonical reference for
              tool-integrated domain agents across the AKD ecosystem.
            </p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd-suite/tree/main/akd-ext" target="_blank" rel="noopener">akd-ext ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* ---- AKD services panel (above the pathway) ---- */
  .pathway-services {
    margin-top: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 22px 24px 24px;
    background: var(--bg-0);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04), 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
  }
  .services-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .services-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .services-head p {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .services-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .services-list li {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 12px 14px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .services-list b {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .services-list span {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .services-list { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .services-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  /* ---- Layout skeleton ---- */
  .pathway-diagram {
    margin-top: 32px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
  }

  /* Start row: full-width featured card */
  .pathway-row--start,
  .pathway-row--end {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .pathway-row--start .pipe-step,
  .pathway-row--end .pipe-step {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  /* Branch row: two columns */
  .pathway-row--branches {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* Branch column */
  .branch {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0;
  }

  /* Branch label tag */
  .branch-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  /* Arrow between cards in a branch */
  .branch-arrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1;
    padding: 6px 0;
  }

  /* ---- Fork / merge indicators ---- */
  .fork-indicator,
  .merge-indicator {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 12px 0;
    gap: 0;
  }
  .fork-line {
    flex: 1;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--border-strong);
  }
  .fork-node {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding: 0 12px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* ---- Card: pipe-step ---- */
  .pipe-step {
    position: relative;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 22px 18px;
    background: var(--bg-0);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04), 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
    text-align: left;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  /* Featured (start / end) card gets a subtle accent top border */
  .pipe-step--featured {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.05), 0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);
  }
  .pipe-step--featured::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 2px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0 0;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--accent), transparent);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .pipe-step b {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 17px;
    display: block;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  .pipe-step span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .pipe-desc {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .pipe-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid oklch(0.546 0.245 262.881 / 0.35);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    margin-top: 4px;
    align-self: flex-start;
    transition: border-bottom-color 0.18s ease, color 0.18s ease;
  }

  /* ---- Governance tag inside each pipe-step ---- */
  .gov-tag {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    background: oklch(0.97 0.005 262.881);
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .gov-tag span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-right: 4px;
  }
  .gov-tag--strong {
    border-left-width: 4px;
    background: oklch(0.95 0.012 262.881);
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .pipe-step--gov-gate {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .pipe-link:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent-4);
  }

  /* ---- Distribution endpoints grid ---- */
  .endpoints-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .pipe-step--endpoint {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }
  .pipe-step--endpoint::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 2px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0 0;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--accent), transparent);
    opacity: 0.4;
  }

  .endpoint-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* ---- Responsive ---- */
  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .endpoints-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .pathway-row--branches {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .pathway-row--start .pipe-step,
    .pathway-row--end .pipe-step {
      max-width: 100%;
    }
    .fork-indicator,
    .merge-indicator {
      max-width: 100%;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 580px) {
    .endpoints-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
